0016:     - Rotate the sprite (0/90/180/270°) so its contact edge has exactly N-2 contiguous cells aligned with the hub side, and the rotated sprite is mirror-symmetric along the contact-edge axis (UD for left/right, LR for top/bottom).
0017:     - Translate it to adjoin that hub side. 
0018:     - Clear everything else to bg; output is hub + attached sprites only.
0019: 
0020:     Key insight: Each edge color uniquely pairs a sprite to a side; symmetry along the contact-edge axis disambiguates the correct rotation.
